// Title: User Added To Root/Sudoers Group Using Usermod
// Sigma ID: 6a50f16c-3b7b-42d1-b081-0fdd3ba70a73
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: TuanLe (GTSC)
// Date: 2022-12-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence
// Description: Detects usage of the "usermod" binary to add users add users to the root or suoders groups
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrator activities
// References:
//   - https://pberba.github.io/security/2021/11/23/linux-threat-hunting-for-persistence-account-creation-manipulation/
//   - https://www.configserverfirewall.com/ubuntu-linux/ubuntu-add-user-to-root-group/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_usermod_susp_group.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/usermod" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-aG root" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-aG sudoers")
